# .claude/devil/critical-globs.conf — the project's critical-path scope.
#
# One glob per line, matched (shell `case` pattern) against repo-relative
# changed-file paths. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# This file is DATA — it is read and matched, never executed.
#
# devil.sh reads it: a diff or wrapup touching a matching path takes the
# strong model lane, escalates codex's reasoning effort and gets
# critical-invariants.md injected into the prompt. Anything else you point at
# this file (an authoring-time hook, a CI check) agrees with the devil by
# construction.
#
# Match whole modules generously — harmless extra hits are cheaper than a
# missed critical file. Agreement between consumers is guaranteed; COVERAGE is
# not: pin it with an anchor test of your own ("every file importing <critical
# helper> must be matched by these globs").
#
# Until this file holds at least one active line, critical-path detection is
# off (devil.sh says so on every diff and wrapup run).
# Examples — uncomment and edit:
#*src/auth/*
#*src/billing/*
#*db/migrations/*
